# Task Gates

1. Read only the project spec and `.cursor/tasks/current-task.md` before implementation.
2. Confirm the active task ID, scope, dependencies, files, acceptance criteria, and test commands.
3. Change its status from `TODO` to `IN_PROGRESS` before editing code.
4. Implement only that task. Record discovered follow-up work under the relevant future task.
5. Review the complete diff for scope creep, regressions, accessibility, responsive behavior, and placeholders.
6. Run every test command listed for the task plus affected project checks.
7. A task may become `REVIEW` only when implementation is complete and all required checks pass.
8. Report changed files, behavior, test commands, results, and remaining risks.
9. Wait for the user to reply `Duyệt Txxx` before changing the task to `DONE` or starting another task.
10. After approval, update the backlog status, copy the next task into `current-task.md`, and then begin a new work cycle.
11. If a test fails, keep the task `IN_PROGRESS`, fix it, and rerun the full gate.
12. Never skip, merge, or reorder tasks without recording the decision and receiving user approval.
13. Do not claim tests passed unless their commands were actually executed successfully.

